Third-Party Data & Engine Attributions:
1. Relate (Neo4j Embedded Graph Database) — used as the single-file ACID graph
   engine (.rl bundles) with live Cypher execution, constraints, and indexes.
2. OpenStreetMap Contributors — road topology, building footprints, services,
   and environmental zones are derived from OpenStreetMap data via Overpass API,
   available under the Open Database License (ODbL 1.0):
   https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
3. Digital Elevation Models (DEM) — terrain elevations are sourced from
   Open-Meteo Copernicus DEM (CC-BY 4.0) and OpenTopoData SRTM 30m fallback.
4. Frontend Visualization — built with React, Vite, MapLibre GL JS, and Deck.gl.
